course: dictionary
lesson: 15853
title: Uneventful: nothing special happens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some days are quiet, and nothing much happens at all. Writers have a word for that: uneventful. «Our long train journey was uneventful, and we arrived on time.» Nothing exciting happened and nothing went wrong. The clues are «long» and «on time»: the journey was boring in the good way, because it all went smoothly.
explain: Uneventful can also be about a job like a doctor's operation. «The doctor said the operation was uneventful.» That is good news. It means there were no problems during the operation, and the patient was safe. Here, uneventful is a calm, happy word.
explain: Try the swap test. Put the meaning into the sentence: «Our long train journey was nothing special or bad, and we arrived on time.» It still makes sense, so you have understood it. Notice the un- at the start: it means not, so uneventful means not full of events.
fact: Uneventful is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a day, a trip or an operation.
fact: «Uneventful» means with nothing special, exciting or bad happening.
fact: For a trip or an operation, «uneventful» means it went smoothly, with no problems.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so «uneventful» is the opposite of «eventful», which means full of things happening.
fact: Its comparative forms are «more uneventful» and «most uneventful».
exercise: «Our long train journey was uneventful, and we arrived on time.» What does uneventful mean here? | Late and cold | Full of exciting things | Very loud and busy | *Nothing went wrong and nothing special happened
exercise: «The doctor said the operation was uneventful.» Is this good or bad news? | Bad news, because it was very dangerous | Bad news, because it was very long | Neither, because it was a secret | *Good news, because there were no problems
exercise: Find and copy one word in this sentence that means not full of events: «The summer was calm and uneventful.» | *uneventful | calm | summer | was
test: «After the storm, the night was quiet and uneventful.» What does uneventful suggest about the night? | It was very cold and windy | It was full of exciting things | *Nothing much happened | Everyone was awake all night
test: The prefix un- means not. If eventful means full of events, what does uneventful mean? | *Not full of events | Happening again and again | Going very fast | Full of very big events
exam: Ruby says, «Our holiday was uneventful, so it must have been full of adventures.» Is Ruby right? | Yes, uneventful means full of adventures | *No, uneventful means nothing special or exciting happened | No, uneventful means it was over very quickly | Yes, uneventful means it was very noisy
